{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tool's `args` schema is passed to LLMs for function calling (via adapters), so excluding the bogus `kwargs` entry is correct behavior — the LLM shouldn't see a `kwargs` parameter.\n\nNow let me implement the fix in `/testbed/dspy/primitives/tool.py`:\n\n1. `_parse_function`:\n   - Detect `VAR_KEYWORD` and store as `self.has_var_keyword`.\n   - Exclude `VAR_POSITIONAL`/`VAR_KEYWORD` params from `hints` and `default_values`.\n\n2. `__call__`:\n   - Allow args not in `self.args` when `self.has_var_keyword` is True; skip type validation for them (no declared type). Keep ValueError otherwise.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The tool's `args` schema is passed to LLMs for function calling (via adapters), so excluding the bogus `kwargs` entry is correct behavior — the LLM shouldn't see a `kwargs` parameter.\\n\\nNow let me implement the fix in `/testbed/dspy/primitives/tool.py`:\\n\\n1. `_parse_function`:\\n   - Detect `VAR_KEYWORD` and store as `self.has_var_keyword`.\\n   - Exclude `VAR_POSITIONAL`/`VAR_KEYWORD` params from `hints` and `default_values`.\\n\\n2. `__call__`:\\n   - Allow args not in `self.args` when `self.has_var_keyword` is True; skip type validation for them (no declared type). Keep ValueError otherwise.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The `args` schema feeds LLM function-calling, so the bogus `kwargs` entry shouldn't be there either. Now I'll implement the fix:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f9ea6a39cdac4849a7ac012f","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/testbed/dspy/primitives/tool.py","edits":[{"oldText":"        # Use inspect.signature to get all arg names\n        sig = inspect.signature(annotations_func)\n        # Get available type hints\n        available_hints = get_type_hints(annotations_func)\n        # Build a dictionary of arg name -> type (defaulting to Any when missing)\n        hints = {param_name: available_hints.get(param_name, Any) for param_name in sig.parameters.keys()}\n        default_values = {param_name: sig.parameters[param_name].default for param_name in sig.parameters.keys()}","newText":"        # Use inspect.signature to get all arg names\n        sig = inspect.signature(annotations_func)\n        # Whether the function accepts arbitrary keyword arguments (e.g. a **kwargs parameter). Such functions\n        # can receive keyword arguments that are not explicitly defined in their signature.\n        self.has_var_keyword = any(\n            param.kind == inspect.Parameter.VAR_KEYWORD for param in sig.parameters.values()\n        )\n        # Get available type hints\n        available_hints = get_type_hints(annotations_func)\n        # Build a dictionary of arg name -> type (defaulting to Any when missing), skipping *args/**kwargs\n        # parameters since they are not concrete, nameable arguments of the function.\n        hints = {\n            param_name: available_hints.get(param_name, Any)\n            for param_name, param in sig.parameters.items()\n            if param.kind not in (inspect.Parameter.VAR_POSITIONAL, inspect.Parameter.VAR_KEYWORD)\n        }\n        default_values = {\n            param_name: sig.parameters[param_name].default\n            for param_name, param in sig.parameters.items()\n            if param.kind not in (inspect.Parameter.VAR_POSITIONAL, inspect.Parameter.VAR_KEYWORD)\n        }"},{"oldText":"    @with_callbacks\n    def __call__(self, **kwargs):\n        for k, v in kwargs.items():\n            if k not in self.args:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Arg {k} is not in the tool's args.\")\n            try:","newText":"    @with_callbacks\n    def __call__(self, **kwargs):\n        for k, v in kwargs.items():\n            if k not in self.args:\n                # If the function accepts arbitrary keyword arguments (e.g. a **kwargs parameter), allow\n                # arguments that are not explicitly defined in its signature to pass through, since the\n                # underlying function is designed to handle them.\n                if self.has_var_keyword:\n                    continue\n                raise ValueError(f\"Arg {k} is not in the tool's args.\")\n            try:"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":345,"output":774,"cacheRead":11968,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":150,"totalTokens":13087,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788462115746,"responseId":"gen-1788462115-Py5k0H2DYC2LJFLaRmQC","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
